362
00:25:49,090 --> 00:25:50,000
Rym: It's kind of like an emulator.

363
00:25:50,200 --> 00:25:51,009
Rym: It mostly just works.

364
00:25:51,453 --> 00:25:52,080
Rym: It's a cool thing.

365
00:25:52,180 --> 00:25:53,020
Rym: We've talked about it before.

366
00:25:54,820 --> 00:26:19,049
Rym: Nintendo in Japan, so the home turf, had to make a different special app for exactly two N64 games separate from the rest of the N64 games that they brought on the Switch because Japan has extremely restrictive and kind of broken censorship and access laws around video games.

367
00:26:19,453 --> 00:26:26,000
Rym: And there are certain things that make a video game basically automatically get classified into this special category.

368
00:26:26,964 --> 00:26:29,399
Rym: Z-rating is two more.

369
00:26:30,361 --> 00:26:36,243
Rym: But a Z-rated game in Japan legally cannot be sold to anyone under 18.

370
00:26:36,243 --> 00:26:50,519
Rym: And as a result, Nintendo had to make a special 18+ only with verification version of the N64 app just for Goldeneye and Jet Force Gemini and no other games.

371
00:26:51,782 --> 00:27:00,424
Scott: It's like, hey, that's, you know, because if you have to put the rate, you know, if they package all those games into one app on the Switch instead of having them be individual.

372
00:27:00,445 --> 00:27:05,456
Rym: The whole app would have to be 18+ or the app would have to have age verification built into it.

373
00:27:06,503 --> 00:27:07,636
Scott: Yeah, or something like that.

374
00:27:07,656 --> 00:27:11,353
Scott: So they just went with the easiest solution to comply with the law.

375
00:27:11,373 --> 00:27:12,099
Scott: Just make two apps.

376
00:27:12,342 --> 00:27:14,380
Scott: It's like, OK, it's probably very easy.

377
00:27:14,500 --> 00:27:16,320
Scott: It's probably a very easy technical solution.

378
00:27:16,381 --> 00:27:19,269
Rym: Yeah, it's a really silly law and I don't want to get into that.

379
00:27:19,310 --> 00:27:20,522
Rym: Like, it's kind of good that the U.S.

380
00:27:20,563 --> 00:27:21,108
Rym: never actually...

381
00:27:21,148 --> 00:27:26,199
Scott: It's so weird how, you know, Japan also, some, you know, some of the things they allow and then don't allow.

382
00:27:27,505 --> 00:27:31,291
Scott: It's like a crazy mixed bag I can't keep track of and I don't because I don't live there.

383
00:27:31,372 --> 00:27:31,554
Scott: Yep.

384
00:27:31,837 --> 00:27:41,107
Rym: Also, most, I would say of all the games affected by the differences in those rules between the U.S.

385
00:27:41,147 --> 00:27:47,257
Rym: and Japan are games that I either have no interest in playing or potentially agenda I have moral questions about.

386
00:27:48,763 --> 00:27:50,299
Rym: But in this case, it's Goldeneye.

387
00:27:52,762 --> 00:28:04,178
Rym: Like... So expect a lot of people going for the low rent joke to talk about the 18+ only N64 app, but all it is is Goldeneye and a game most of you have never heard of.

